    "The gpt-5.6 family uses size codenames (sol/terra/luna) instead of the -mini/-nano suffixes of earlier generations. Guessing the old pattern gives a model id that does not exist.",
    "The 5.4/5.5/5.6 families publish a separate cache-WRITE price at 1.25x base input, on top of the cache-read price recorded in cached_input. Older families publish no cache-write rate.",
    "Batch and flex service tiers are half the standard rate; priority is double. Verified for the 5.6 family only.",
    "gpt-5.4 and gpt-5.5 rates are published for prompts under 272K context; no rate above that is published.",
